  message: "PREMISE AUDIT 2026-10-03 (owner-requested; read-only, reproduced at dev 3abedae588 on small fixtures). PARTLY STALE: core claim holds, size and context outdated. Title updated.\n- scip/index.py:407 still sets stable_id=_short_sha256(sym_info.symbol). On the raw SCIP output: 2 colliding groups, 5 records (crate/ in build.rs, src/main.rs, src/lib.rs; main(). in build.rs and src/main.rs).\n- AFTER THE ADR-0057 MERGE (WI-kokiz, PR 1072): the two main records pair with tree-sitter twins and take the tree-sitter stable_id. After the merge + split_within_file_stable_id_collisions, ONE group remains: sha256:fe9021ce48cd040c, the three SCIP-only crate/ namespace records (cross-file, so the within-file splitter returns 0). So \"5 of 756\" is now \"3 records in one group, of 169 after the merge\".\n- MOOT: \"INV-dolud's parity question should be settled first\": INV-dolud is satisfied and ADR-0057 decides merged records keep the incumbent's id. Fix option (a) (path into the hash) now changes only SCIP-only records and alternative values on merged records. WI-talos stays relevant.\n- NOT CHECKED: a full survey with the backend on (runs rust-analyzer)."  # 33dd
